grub-once for Debian
--------------------

grub-once reads /boot/grub/grub.cfg and sets the boot entry that is
used for the next boot only (via grub-reboot / the next_entry variable
in /boot/grub/grubenv).

Usage:

  grub-once --list            list all boot entries
  grub-once --enum            list entries with their grub id
  grub-once ID                boot entry with number ID once
  grub-once NAME_SUBSTRING    boot the first entry matching the substring

The accompanying grub-once.service removes next_entry again after the
boot if GRUB itself could not update the environment block (e.g. when
/boot is on LVM, mdraid or btrfs), so the selection really applies to
one boot only. For this to work, GRUB_DEFAULT in /etc/default/grub
must be "saved".

